
2.2.1. Usage of strcat() function
01:16
Write a C program that reads two strings 
 and 
 from the user and concatenates two strings using the strcat() function.



Input Format:

The first line contains the first string 
 (up to 99 characters).
The second line contains the second string 
 (up to 99 characters).


#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
	char str1[100];  // First string
	char str2[100];  // Second string


    // Read input strings
    scanf("%s", str1);
    scanf("%s", str2);

    // Concatenate str2 to str1
    strcat(str1, str2);

	// Print the concatenated result
	printf("%s\n", str1);
	
	return 0;
}

